WEBVTT

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:07.150
My beloved fatherland, I have returned!

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:11.490
How I've longed to see you, Lord Richmond!

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:12.650
No,

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:14.450
my king!

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:16.820
Stanley.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:19.990
Where is your stepson Richmond?

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:25.000
I will mete out death to traitors,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.090
be they great lords, close relatives,

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:29.880
or intimate friends.

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.920
It matters not how well I loved them.

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:34.130
I make no exceptions.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:38.970
My lords!

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:43.480
We must fortify the crown so that
no one will ever again foment rebellion!

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:46.730
I shall bolster the royal forces

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:50.070
and adjudicate rights and
arms with greater severity!

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:53.190
I will not have charlatans
counterfeiting lineage

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:56.780
and armorial bearings to lay
false claim to royal blood!

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:03.700
There must be no exceptions.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:07.540
I slew even my other half
with my own hands.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:09.420
Richard,

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:12.460
would you make a few moments for me?

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:20.680
York of the white rose.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:23.310
Lancaster of the red rose.

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:29.730
These royal houses with roses for
their crests battled for the throne.

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:34.440
People call their strife
the "Wars of the Roses."

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:12.880
Don't go deep into the forest,
and don't make a fuss.

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:13.880
I won't.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:16.420
It's been so long

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:19.720
since you and I visited
the woods like this.

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:21.800
Somehow, it all seems like a dream.

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:27.140
The rain has long since ceased,

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:29.100
yet I search wherever I go.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:34.150
It's all a bad dream.

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:35.150
Anne?

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:40.440
It's not just the battlefield,
or the councils or feasts.

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:43.280
A royal palace isn't right for Edward.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:45.030
What's come over you?

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:47.620
Please, Richard.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:50.500
Disinherit him.

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:52.210
What do you--

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:56.590
I haven't long to live.

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:59.670
I had an attack of
tuberculosis as a child.

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:01.970
Now I have it again.

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:03.430
You recovered once before.

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:06.350
I know my own body better than--

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:09.100
Anne!

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:13.810
I thought that I'd be able to shape
this kingdom alongside you.

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:18.110
I thought that I'd be able
to guard Edward's future.

00:04:18.110 --> 00:04:22.650
Even if I die, the threats
to his life will continue.

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:27.830
As long as he's a king's son, he's doomed
to a life of blood and conspiracy.

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:29.790
You made certain of that!

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:32.040
Didn't you, Richard?

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:33.160
Why?

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:35.120
Set Edward free

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:38.420
from the curse of this
dreadful circlet of light.

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:42.720
Why is God so insatiable?

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:44.720
Why does He keep taking from me?

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:49.850
My whole body is on the verge of freezing.

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:55.100
Next time, make a true heir
with someone you can truly love.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:56.600
No! This is wrong!

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:58.520
This isn't the place!

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:01.360
The king's bed can't be this cold.

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:04.860
Where?

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:08.120
Where is he?

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:15.660
Why isn't he here?

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.370
How can he not be here?!

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:19.630
Your Majesty?

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:24.670
He's...

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:27.090
He's gone!

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:29.930
Yet I can't sleep without him.

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:31.140
Your Majesty.

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:33.270
Call me "Richard."

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:34.890
Like he did.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:39.020
I want... that heat.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:41.070
K-King Richard.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:45.440
Just close your eyes.
Imagine the woman you fancy.

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:46.740
King Richard!

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:50.030
We can't.

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:53.450
Heat of the flesh can't warm your soul.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:56.540
I know.

00:05:56.540 --> 00:06:00.380
No one knows that better than me.

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:02.170
I want to see him.

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:04.710
But he's gone.

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:07.170
Because I loved him.

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:09.680
All I love is vanishing.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:13.760
Everything I care for will be gone.

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:17.640
I sinned to obtain my desire.

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:22.110
Is all this the wages of sin?

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:24.150
King Richard,

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:26.900
I'll stay with you to the last.

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:37.620
My sovereign, I have
something to show you.

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:38.710
And that is?

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:44.340
This is the purpose that the Duke
of Buckingham entrusted to me.

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:47.760
Lord Oxford,

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:52.890
our army is safe in the hands
of a veteran such as yourself.

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:56.470
But we are not yet heroes.

00:06:56.470 --> 00:07:00.190
Richard can claim to be
the legitimate king.

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:02.190
And what of our forces?

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:03.400
Foreigners!

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:05.020
Traitors!

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:09.400
Richmond, whose claim to the
throne is, frankly, rather dubious.

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:11.320
It's too late for such worries.

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:16.080
What do you think we
need to make us heroes?

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:17.370
Power?

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:18.950
Victory?

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:21.620
And a story.

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:25.840
Come one, come all!

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:28.840
The show's about to start!

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:29.800
Actors?

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:34.970
Yes. Heroism requires one thing above all.

00:07:34.970 --> 00:07:36.260
--Namely...
--Here, we shall reenact the hidden
truth of the royal palace!

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:39.480
--Here, we shall reenact the hidden
truth of the royal palace!

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:41.060
Its cursed reality!

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:42.650
A consummate...

00:07:42.650 --> 00:07:46.770
The wicked tale of King Richard III!

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:51.030
...villain!

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:56.740
A nightingale?

00:07:56.740 --> 00:07:58.790
Did it wander here out of season?

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:04.790
What will burial benefit a soulless brute?

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:09.090
Only human beings may enter
the Kingdom of Heaven.

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:12.170
Your Majesty, I bear fresh tidings!

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:16.930
The Earl of Richmond's army
has come ashore in Wales!

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:19.970
So, Richmond has come at last.

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:24.730
The Earl of Oxford and several
other lords have joined his cause.

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:26.730
Shall I summon the council?

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:28.730
Deliberation is pointless.

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:32.650
We have no choice but to give battle!

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:36.660
Have you heard?
Sympathizers are flocking to his banner.

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:40.240
The king might fall if nothing is done.

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:45.170
Lord Stanley, if you go southwest,
we would be happy to--

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:46.580
My lords!

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:51.590
I take it you're so well prepared
for war that you have time for gossip?

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:55.010
N-Not quite. I must depart
to ready my forces!

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:58.430
And I must levy troops.

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:01.060
Ungrateful fair-weather friends.

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:04.520
Still, considering this
string of rebellions...

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:07.310
How can you join in such talk?!

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:09.570
I can't help feeling uneasy.

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:12.110
Ever since the war with Buckingham,

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:14.030
the king has been a shell of himself.

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:18.950
My health hasn't returned.

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:22.120
Is that medicine to blame? Or is it...

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:23.370
King Richard!

00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:24.830
King Richard!

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:26.460
Richard.

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:29.250
Richard!

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:33.420
They're all looking for
a chance to turn on you.

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:36.510
Incessant rebellions. A dying queen.

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:39.720
If you lose your precious heir as well,

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:42.470
you'll lose everything.

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:46.190
Even the crown you killed
your other half to keep.

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:51.270
How is Her Majesty?

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:53.280
She's stable now,

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:56.740
but to be honest, the end
could come at any time.

00:09:56.740 --> 00:10:01.120
And the Prince of Wales shows
symptoms of the same disease.

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:11.090
If you let that boy go,
you have no future.

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:13.630
I'm well aware of that.

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:19.590
Joan, you've made just one error.

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:23.180
What I sought to protect
at any cost was...

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:26.640
Anne?!

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:29.060
Mother?! Where are you going?!

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:33.150
That place is too haunted by death!

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:35.190
This is my only chance to flee!

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:36.320
Please wait!

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:37.240
Mother!

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:41.570
Everyone will worry. Let's turn back.

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:43.700
Listen, Edward.

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:46.250
I'm going... to die soon.

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:48.210
D-Die?

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:53.790
When I'm gone, the palace will be
a den of those who wish you dead.

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:57.170
Especially if Richard loses his war.

00:10:57.170 --> 00:11:02.090
The king's son will be executed, or else
imprisoned for the rest of his days.

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:03.140
Before that happens--

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:04.760
Anne! Wait!

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:05.890
Father.

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:09.640
No!

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:11.560
No!

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:13.400
I can't stay here!

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:18.070
This place--that palace--
isn't what I hoped for!

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:19.360
Anne.

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:20.780
I want to go back.

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:24.330
Back to the way I was
before I met you that day!

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:27.790
Back to who I was
before my life was stolen!

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:29.750
Wait, Anne!

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:32.500
I wasn't even allowed to dream.

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:34.000
A woman's duty

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:37.340
is merely to love whoever
is placed before her.

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:42.430
Anne...

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:45.010
Let go.

00:11:46.060 --> 00:11:47.970
Listen, Richard.

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:51.560
You are... my curse.

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:54.020
And not because I loved you.

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:57.020
I wasn't bound because I loved you,

00:11:57.020 --> 00:11:59.230
but because I wanted you to love me.

00:11:59.230 --> 00:12:03.990
All this time,
you wouldn't even fetter me.

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:06.780
I bound myself with briars.

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:11.410
Her every wish for love

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:15.500
nurtured briars to tie her down.

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:22.220
You wanted to be loved.

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:23.430
Richard.

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:25.590
Anne, I'm sorry.

00:12:27.550 --> 00:12:29.720
Here and now,

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:32.480
let's cut through those briars together.

00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:40.690
I chose a bloody path of my own free will.

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:43.650
You needn't burden yourself with my fate.

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:52.000
Edward,

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:55.370
I love you.

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:58.710
Even if it costs me everything.

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:05.180
Once he's clear of London,
announce that the Prince of Wales is dead.

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:09.050
I want to hold his
"funeral" before the war.

00:13:09.050 --> 00:13:12.140
Is this... a letter from Anne?

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:14.230
Why is the seal unbroken?

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:31.490
Was that really for the best?

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:34.960
The death of an heir
is a fatal blow to a king.

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:37.120
If your wife were to pass as well...

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:38.750
Silence!

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:41.590
Anne <i>will</i> pull through.

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:46.550
You know she won't. Isn't that why
you want to grant her wish?

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:50.100
Now her wish is mine as well.

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:54.310
Give this to Edward for me.

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:57.350
It's a memento of his father.

00:13:57.350 --> 00:14:01.190
Jane, take good care of Edward--

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:04.690
I mean, of that nameless boy.

00:14:06.610 --> 00:14:08.820
Your Majesty! You mustn't enter!

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:11.240
If you catch the queen's illness--

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:14.790
Stand aside! Anne is my wife!

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:16.870
Richard.

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:21.000
Lie down, Anne. This isn't good for you.

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:24.630
We didn't lose that boy,

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:25.800
did we?

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:31.260
No, he gained a new life.

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:32.550
Thank you.

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:33.560
Anne!

00:14:34.770 --> 00:14:36.770
Richard...

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:39.480
Now I can die peacefully.

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:42.980
Don't talk nonsense. You'll get well soon.

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:45.730
I'll host a feast to
celebrate your recovery.

00:14:45.730 --> 00:14:48.610
I'll even have a new dress made for you.

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:53.780
You wear the dress.
I like how you look in one.

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:57.540
I'll grant your every desire.

00:14:57.540 --> 00:15:01.210
No wish is beyond the king's power.

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:05.340
Your Majesty,

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:10.180
I am deeply grateful for
your boundless kindness.

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:13.470
You even provided my daughter
with this lovely dress.

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:16.180
It was all Anne's wish.

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:19.180
I had that dress made for her.

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:22.150
I'm sure she would be
pleased to see you wear it.

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:27.740
How do you expect me to look
Uncle Richard in the eye?

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:30.240
I'm engaged to his enemy!

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:32.910
But not wedded to him.

00:15:32.910 --> 00:15:35.700
Queen Anne will soon be dead.

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:39.660
Thus, Richard desires your bloodline.

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:40.710
He wouldn't!

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:43.880
This is all for your happiness.

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:47.760
If you wish to return to the palace,
I will go with you.

00:15:47.760 --> 00:15:49.550
After all,

00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:52.590
you're my last ray of hope.

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:56.350
Uncle!

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:05.610
No matter how much ill people speak
of you, I won't believe them!

00:16:08.070 --> 00:16:11.530
I pray that your life will be blessed

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:15.280
and that you live out your
full span of years in peace.

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:19.040
Edward was always concerned for you.

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:20.580
Richard,

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:25.960
perhaps you really did free us out
of the goodness of your heart.

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:32.170
But with that kind whim,
you dug your own grave!

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:35.390
My name is Henry Tudor, Earl of Richmond!

00:16:35.390 --> 00:16:38.970
I have come to reclaim England from you!

00:16:38.970 --> 00:16:40.770
My brave and earnest gentlemen!

00:16:40.770 --> 00:16:46.860
Please, lend Richmond your strength
to dethrone this demon king!

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:49.320
Down with Richard III!

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:51.820
Demon! Demon! Demon!

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:02.250
Dear Duke Richard,

00:17:02.250 --> 00:17:05.960
Do you remember that day at the banquet?

00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:11.550
I was truly glad that you asked
me to dance with you then.

00:17:11.550 --> 00:17:15.970
It's strange. When I picture
you in my mind's eye,

00:17:15.970 --> 00:17:20.430
I soar out of the darkness,
like a skylark at dawn.

00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:25.980
How I would love to dance
with you again someday.

00:17:25.980 --> 00:17:29.060
Until that day comes,

00:17:29.060 --> 00:17:32.320
I pray for your happiness.

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:44.120
Brave soldiers of England!

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:49.170
The traitor Richmond now seeks
to usurp our rightful throne!

00:17:49.170 --> 00:17:53.010
He devastates our land in
his march toward London!

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:58.220
But our foes are beaten curs
who once fled England in defeat!

00:17:58.220 --> 00:18:01.720
A common thorn has more power to wound us!

00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:05.060
We are the righteous
shield of our fatherland!

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:07.770
In the name of your king, to battle!

00:18:07.770 --> 00:18:09.440
Advance!

00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:13.650
Even if God watches over Richmond,

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:16.700
there are no more briars in my path.

00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:19.820
There's nothing left to me.

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:21.080
What are you doing?!

00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:22.620
--Make way!
--Impertinent wretch!

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:25.160
Do you know to whom you speak?!

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:27.790
I am the mother of your king!

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:33.340
Have you come to pray
for victory in battle?

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:35.590
I have indeed.

00:18:35.590 --> 00:18:37.760
For Richmond's victory.

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:40.430
Then kindly stand aside, Mother.

00:18:40.430 --> 00:18:41.930
Beat the marching drums!

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:43.470
Richard.

00:18:43.470 --> 00:18:46.020
The day you were born...

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:49.900
A terrible storm laid trees low.

00:18:49.900 --> 00:18:53.320
Owls screeched.
Crows croaked in the night!

00:18:53.320 --> 00:18:57.990
Your mother suffered
abnormal birthing pains!

00:18:57.990 --> 00:19:01.240
And after all that, her child was...

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:05.410
...a blood-soaked demon
that defied the will of God!

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:12.670
So, this voice that always tormented me

00:19:12.670 --> 00:19:16.170
was yours all along.

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:20.590
Richard, you are unfit to be king.

00:19:20.590 --> 00:19:23.800
I should have been
truthful before it came to this.

00:19:23.800 --> 00:19:28.430
I should have revealed our secret,
which I'd hoped to take to my grave.

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:31.850
Your father

00:19:31.850 --> 00:19:35.520
was not Richard Plantagenet, Duke of York.

00:19:39.450 --> 00:19:43.450
I have no more time
to waste on your ravings.

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:46.910
Ten months and ten days before your birth,

00:19:46.910 --> 00:19:49.370
during our days of strife with Lancaster,

00:19:49.370 --> 00:19:53.920
my husband Richard was
overcome by rage and desperation.

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:58.420
Between that pressure and his lust
for the crown, he had no place for me.

00:19:58.420 --> 00:19:59.800
So I...

00:19:59.800 --> 00:20:01.720
I...

00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:04.760
You look nothing like
your father or brothers.

00:20:04.760 --> 00:20:07.720
Everything about you is proof of my deed!

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:13.940
True, I don't resemble Father.

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:18.150
But I'm just like you, Mother!

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:21.450
We clung to what we could never have

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:25.700
and punished ourselves to
escape our senseless suffering.

00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:28.370
We called ourselves sinners and demons.

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:31.120
We could never have endured it otherwise!

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:32.370
No!

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:34.670
Mother,

00:20:34.670 --> 00:20:37.380
you are no sinner.

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:39.920
You're a victim.

00:20:41.630 --> 00:20:45.050
No! I am no victim!

00:20:45.050 --> 00:20:47.050
I sinned!

00:20:47.050 --> 00:20:50.270
Your birth was my punishment!

00:20:50.270 --> 00:20:53.640
Although my husband always loved me,

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:56.650
he... he...

00:20:56.650 --> 00:21:00.990
He refused to love my darkness.

00:21:00.990 --> 00:21:04.070
How slender and frail she is.

00:21:04.070 --> 00:21:07.450
She's small, like I am.

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:10.950
Have I been under this
person's sway all this time?

00:21:12.250 --> 00:21:16.130
Mother, please pray.

00:21:16.130 --> 00:21:18.380
Pray for Richmond's triumph

00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:19.800
and my death.

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:25.340
I hope that will be a comfort to you.

00:21:25.340 --> 00:21:27.720
For all my hatred,

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:29.470
I...

00:21:29.470 --> 00:21:32.470
In truth, I always...

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:40.570
Mother...

00:21:40.570 --> 00:21:41.730
Goodbye.

00:21:43.150 --> 00:21:46.490
Goodbye, my "curse."
